{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC evidence — measured on the landed tree at `693030cb9ab` (worktree `impl-19c3`)\n\n### AC1 — no deleted filename still referenced — MET\n\nRan the AC's own word-anchored form, `git grep -nE \"(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])<basename>\"`, across all 22 removed basenames over the whole tree excluding `.test_durations`.\n\n**Exactly 1 hit, and it is the one already recorded:** `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/code_arrow.json:16` — `test_gate_error_sidecar_heldout.py`, appearing as pytest node ids inside a captured failure transcript in a frozen corpus fixture. That is the literal named in the \"Frozen literals and the anchoring fix\" comment. **Zero hits for the other 21 basenames.**\n\nThe `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` stale row the AC also exempts produced **no hit**, because this commit drained it (see AC5) — the exemption turned out not to be needed.\n\n**The amendment's premise reproduces exactly.** Running the *unanchored* `git grep -F` form alongside it, `test_registry_heldout.py` returns 2 extra hits at `tests/unit/test_attest_registry.py:14,:84`. Both are substring matches inside `test_attest_registry_heldout.py` — \"attest\" ends in \"test\", so the longer name contains the shorter one at index 7 — and both lines are S1 `361f`'s provenance comments, which no work on this story could clear. Anchoring removes both. The amendment was correct.\n\n### AC2 — both vocabulary/mechanism gates exit 0 — MET\n\n`check_mechanism_delta.py --check` → `rc=0`; `check_criteria_vocabulary.py` → `rc=0`.\n\n### AC3 — zero paired twins remain — MET\n\nLooped all 22 pairs; `git ls-files <base>_heldout.py` printed nothing for every one. **Remaining paired twins: 0.**\n\n### AC4 — per-pair node counts reconcile — MET\n\nRecorded earlier on this ticket: **22 pairs, 0 mismatches, 237 → 237.**\n\n### AC5 — mechanism delta + baseline drain — MET for the committed-drain half\n\n`check_mechanism_delta.py --check` → `rc=0`. The drain the AC requires is in this commit's diff of `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (1 deletion, nothing else touched):\n\n```\n-    \"autouse_fixture::tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_backend_scalar_surface_heldout.py::_clean\": 1,\n```\n\n`grep -c 'backend_scalar_surface_heldout' .github/mechanism-baseline.json` → **0**. The surviving base module's identical `_clean` row remains, so the merge deduplicated 2 identical declarations rather than removing a mechanism — which is why this is a `--update-stale` drain and not a baseline edit.\n\n`pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py` is **not** reported separately here on purpose: `make verify` runs it, and running it concurrently against this worktree while the verify is mid-flight would contend for the same tree. Its result arrives with AC6 rather than as a second, weaker measurement.\n\n### AC6 — `make verify` green — IN FLIGHT\n\nRunning in this worktree, at 80%.\n\n---\n\nOutstanding on this ticket: AC6 only. ACs 1–5 are met on the landed tree."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793510908321804711,"uuid":"0ef631ce-f0e6-4cd5-806c-adaba6c580de"}